<rss version="2.0" xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/"><channel><title>News Releases - NVIDIA Newsroom</title><link>https://nvidianews.nvidia.com</link><description>All News</description><language>en-us</language><pubDate>Tue, 13 Oct 2026 18:10:11 GMT</pubDate><lastBuildDate>Tue, 13 Oct 2026 18:10:11 GMT</lastBuildDate><generator>iPressroom</generator><item><title>All Systems Go: Global PC App Ecosystem Ready for NVIDIA RTX Spark</title><link>https://blogs.nvidia.com/blog/local-ai-rtx-spark-laptops-software-updates/</link><media:content url="https://iprsoftwaremedia.com/219/files/202610/bbc6b9cdf14fbe5f7664f977c0ea5447/6ace1dde3d63325cfcf07f50_nv-raig-weekly-kit-10132026-nv-blog-1280x680-1-842x450/nv-raig-weekly-kit-10132026-nv-blog-1280x680-1-842x450_thmb.jpg?v=3d8579af-d065-4e3d-8444-5cd8f6dbb823" fileSize="54806" type="image/jpeg"></media:content><contentType>releases</contentType><image>&lt;img src="https://iprsoftwaremedia.com/219/files/202610/bbc6b9cdf14fbe5f7664f977c0ea5447/6ace1dde3d63325cfcf07f50_nv-raig-weekly-kit-10132026-nv-blog-1280x680-1-842x450/nv-raig-weekly-kit-10132026-nv-blog-1280x680-1-842x450_thmb.jpg?v=3d8579af-d065-4e3d-8444-5cd8f6dbb823" alt="nv-raig-weekly-kit-10132026-nv-blog-1280x680-1-842x450" align="left" hspace="15" vspace="5" /&gt;</image><subtitle></subtitle><categories><category>Blogs</category></categories><modDate>Tue, 13 Oct 2026 12:02:42 GMT</modDate><relatedPages></relatedPages><description><![CDATA[NVIDIA RTX Spark is a new beginning for the PC — a reinvention combining the capabilities of a gaming PC, a creative studio and a personal AI supercomputer into a single superchip. With up to 128GB of unified memory and 1 petaflop of AI compute, RTX Spark delivers the full stack of NVIDIA RTX and […]]]></description><author>Gerardo Delgado</author><guid isPermaLink="true">https://blogs.nvidia.com/blog/local-ai-rtx-spark-laptops-software-updates/</guid><pubDate>Tue, 13 Oct 2026 12:00:49 GMT</pubDate></item><item><title>NVIDIA Lands in Europe for GTC Berlin</title><link>https://blogs.nvidia.com/gtc-berlin-2026-news/</link><media:content url="https://iprsoftwaremedia.com/219/files/20269/576359a162f64f9983d9b3de77530626/6acdbe983d633269055dc501_france-germany-european-commission-collaboration-social-1920x1080-5822338/france-germany-european-commission-collaboration-social-1920x1080-5822338_thmb.jpg?v=e3a43c90-678d-4e4d-b18a-856b0f5a0df1" fileSize="573324" type="image/jpeg"></media:content><contentType>releases</contentType><image>&lt;img src="https://iprsoftwaremedia.com/219/files/20269/576359a162f64f9983d9b3de77530626/6acdbe983d633269055dc501_france-germany-european-commission-collaboration-social-1920x1080-5822338/france-germany-european-commission-collaboration-social-1920x1080-5822338_thmb.jpg?v=e3a43c90-678d-4e4d-b18a-856b0f5a0df1" alt="france-germany-european-commission-collaboration-social-1920x1080-5822338" align="left" hspace="15" vspace="5" /&gt;</image><subtitle></subtitle><categories><category>Blogs</category></categories><modDate>Tue, 13 Oct 2026 05:21:42 GMT</modDate><relatedPages></relatedPages><description><![CDATA[NVIDIA is in Europe, showcasing the future of technology together with the region’s developers, researchers and industry leaders.]]></description><author>NVIDIA Writers</author><guid isPermaLink="true">https://blogs.nvidia.com/gtc-berlin-2026-news/</guid><pubDate>Tue, 13 Oct 2026 05:13:00 GMT</pubDate></item><item><title>From Earth to Orbit, France’s Ecosystem Delivers Agentic Computing at Scale With NVIDIA</title><link>https://blogs.nvidia.com/blog/france-ecosystem-agentic-computing/</link><media:content url="https://iprsoftwaremedia.com/219/files/202610/f62fea35eec4b9278b81b95a5670bff3/6acdbb0e3d63327665b4e82e_france-ai-ecosystem-gtc-berlin-updated-842x450/france-ai-ecosystem-gtc-berlin-updated-842x450_thmb.jpg?v=f8e7dd8e-6113-46c6-bc47-ab9f7abd3a0d" fileSize="15204" type="image/jpeg"></media:content><contentType>releases</contentType><image>&lt;img src="https://iprsoftwaremedia.com/219/files/202610/f62fea35eec4b9278b81b95a5670bff3/6acdbb0e3d63327665b4e82e_france-ai-ecosystem-gtc-berlin-updated-842x450/france-ai-ecosystem-gtc-berlin-updated-842x450_thmb.jpg?v=f8e7dd8e-6113-46c6-bc47-ab9f7abd3a0d" alt="france-ai-ecosystem-gtc-berlin-updated-842x450" align="left" hspace="15" vspace="5" /&gt;</image><subtitle></subtitle><categories><category>Blogs</category></categories><modDate>Tue, 13 Oct 2026 05:01:05 GMT</modDate><relatedPages></relatedPages><description><![CDATA[Companies in France are deploying agentic computing across industries spanning space, financial services, the public sector and scientific research, demonstrating how the country’s ecosystem has moved from ambition to application.  France’s progress sits on deliberate groundwork.  The AI Action Summit in February 2025 and Choose France Summits in 2025 and 2026 anchored major compute commitments […]]]></description><author>Nat Ives</author><guid isPermaLink="true">https://blogs.nvidia.com/blog/france-ecosystem-agentic-computing/</guid><pubDate>Tue, 13 Oct 2026 05:00:31 GMT</pubDate></item><item><title>OCP Global Summit: Amid Ecosystem Adoption, NVIDIA Opens Vera Rubin Architecture to Help Scale AI Factories Worldwide</title><link>https://blogs.nvidia.com/blog/ocp-global-summit-vera-rubin-scale-ai-factories/</link><media:content url="https://iprsoftwaremedia.com/219/files/202610/b714aa393d1a3d790925deb8cbedf198/6accf62c3d6332b0a1302305_gpu-architecture-rolling-blog-kv-ocp-blog-1920x1080-5820310-842x450/gpu-architecture-rolling-blog-kv-ocp-blog-1920x1080-5820310-842x450_thmb.jpg?v=153b22de-a263-454a-98d0-56e9978185ba" fileSize="128393" type="image/jpeg"></media:content><contentType>releases</contentType><image>&lt;img src="https://iprsoftwaremedia.com/219/files/202610/b714aa393d1a3d790925deb8cbedf198/6accf62c3d6332b0a1302305_gpu-architecture-rolling-blog-kv-ocp-blog-1920x1080-5820310-842x450/gpu-architecture-rolling-blog-kv-ocp-blog-1920x1080-5820310-842x450_thmb.jpg?v=153b22de-a263-454a-98d0-56e9978185ba" alt="gpu-architecture-rolling-blog-kv-ocp-blog-1920x1080-5820310-842x450" align="left" hspace="15" vspace="5" /&gt;</image><subtitle></subtitle><categories><category>Blogs</category></categories><modDate>Mon, 12 Oct 2026 15:01:04 GMT</modDate><relatedPages></relatedPages><description><![CDATA[As AI factories grow from megawatts to gigawatts, building them takes more than advanced computing. Open standards are helping the industry scale AI infrastructure faster, more efficiently and more reliably. At the Open Compute Project (OCP) Global Summit, taking place in the San Jose McEnery Convention Center, NVIDIA announced new partnerships and contributions aimed at […]]]></description><author>NVIDIA Writers</author><guid isPermaLink="true">https://blogs.nvidia.com/blog/ocp-global-summit-vera-rubin-scale-ai-factories/</guid><pubDate>Mon, 12 Oct 2026 15:00:25 GMT</pubDate></item><item><title>NVIDIA and Cisco Introduce New Pluggable Optics Form Factor to Scale AI Factories</title><link>https://nvidianews.nvidia.com/news/nvidia-and-cisco-introduce-new-pluggable-optics-form-factor-to-scale-ai-factories</link><media:content url="https://iprsoftwaremedia.com/219/files/202610/bb0658e6668adfadaaf0477f22795d99/6acb0cef3d63325ab15dc4ff_ultra-dense-small-form-factor-pluggable/ultra-dense-small-form-factor-pluggable_thmb.jpg?v=6511e202-6a08-4834-996a-ced5c6faeac3" fileSize="320326" type="image/jpeg"></media:content><contentType>releases</contentType><image>&lt;img src="https://iprsoftwaremedia.com/219/files/202610/bb0658e6668adfadaaf0477f22795d99/6acb0cef3d63325ab15dc4ff_ultra-dense-small-form-factor-pluggable/ultra-dense-small-form-factor-pluggable_thmb.jpg?v=6511e202-6a08-4834-996a-ced5c6faeac3" alt="Ultra-Dense Small Factor Pluggable" align="left" hspace="15" vspace="5" /&gt;</image><subtitle>New Transceivers Enable AI Builders to Scale Compute Within the Same Network Footprint While Reducing Networking’s Share of the Power Budget</subtitle><content>&lt;![CDATA[&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;News Summary:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li style="margin-top:0in; margin-bottom:0.0001pt;"&gt;Ultra-Dense Small Form Factor Pluggable (USFP) is designed to be the first module to support 400Gb/s-per-lane electrical signals, enabling capacity up to 12.8Tb/s so AI factory builders can scale Ethernet AI fabrics, while extending a proven deployment model across multiple generations of data center networks.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li style="margin-top:0in; margin-bottom:0.0001pt;"&gt;USFP delivers 4x the bandwidth density and 1.3x the power efficiency of 200Gb/s-per-lane optics so AI factories can connect more computing systems without adding network tiers, while using less power to move each bit of data.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li style="margin-top:0in; margin-bottom:0.0001pt;"&gt;NVIDIA and Cisco are working with TE Connectivity and Amphenol to build a multi-source hardware ecosystem around USFP.&lt;br /&gt;
	&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;NVIDIA and Cisco today announced plans for Ultra-Dense Small Form Factor Pluggable (USFP), a new high-density 400Gb/s-per-lane optical module designed to equip the hardware ecosystem for the next generation of AI factories using pluggable transceivers.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;As AI models grow and inference demand expands, AI factories must connect more computing systems while managing network complexity, power and costs. Moving more data per watt and per switch helps operators make better use of their infrastructure investments.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Scaling AI factories requires more bandwidth per connection and more connections per switch. When a switch reaches its capacity, further network expansion can require additional switch layers and optical links, increasing latency, power consumption and costs.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;USFP is designed to enable AI factory builders to scale from 200 Gb/s per lane to 400Gb/s-per-lane Ethernet AI fabrics, while extending a deployment model proven at scale across multiple generations of data center networks. With USFP, customers can embrace next-generation optical technology and meet the performance demand of AI workloads without overhauling their data center infrastructure.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The first planned USFP-based transceivers will pack 16 full-duplex lanes in an octal small form factor (OSFP)-sized footprint supporting both switches and SuperNICs, with the ability to expand to 32 and more lanes in the future. By doubling both the lane count and bandwidth per lane, USFP enables AI fabrics to connect more 1.6Tb/s endpoints without adding network tiers. Customers will be able to achieve 12.8Tb/s of overall capacity with USFP.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Comparable with an OSFP-sized module, it delivers 4x the bandwidth and front-panel bandwidth density, with approximately 1.3x the power efficiency, versus 200Gb/s-per-lane pluggable modules. This means AI builders can increase their compute scale within the same network footprint, while decreasing networking&amp;rsquo;s share of the overall AI factory power budget.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&amp;ldquo;Building the world&amp;rsquo;s largest AI factories starts with rethinking the smallest of connections,&amp;rdquo; said Gilad Shainer, senior vice president NVIDIA. &amp;ldquo;With USFP, NVIDIA and Cisco are building an ecosystem to reinvent pluggable optics &amp;mdash; connecting more computing with greater efficiency to power the next generation of AI factories.&amp;rdquo;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&amp;ldquo;AI builders need an interconnect architecture that can scale performance without locking them into a more complex operating model,&amp;rdquo; said Bill Gartner, senior vice president and general manager of optical systems and optics at Cisco. &amp;ldquo;Cisco and NVIDIA recognized that scaling pluggable optics to 400Gb/s per lane would require more than another incremental extension of today&amp;rsquo;s module designs. Through our collaboration, USFP is designed to deliver a new level of bandwidth density while preserving the serviceability, deployment flexibility and operational simplicity of pluggable optics. By taking a full-stack approach &amp;mdash; from silicon and systems to optics and the network operating system &amp;mdash; we can optimize every layer to deliver the performance and scale the next generation of AI networks will require.&amp;rdquo;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;More AI Infrastructure From Every Switch&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br /&gt;
Designed for electrical signals of 400Gb/s per lane, USFP uses a new two-dimensional array connector with a two-step insertion design that engages high-speed contacts after the module is inserted, reducing contact wear, improving signal integrity and making insertion force more predictable. The connector technology allows for further scaling of lane count to 32 full duplex lanes and more in the future. Because the connector is designed for 400Gb/s performance, it also offers improved performance at 200Gb/s per lane.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;USFP supports power dissipation of up to 100 watts without needing a separate, dedicated embedded cooling circuit within the transceiver, reducing switch design complexity and improving reliability. Together, these capabilities enable higher-bandwidth fabrics while preserving the mature deployment, serviceability and manufacturability of existing pluggable transceivers.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;All USFP configurations support optical designs that reduce latency and power consumption by simplifying signal processing. Support for a broad range of optical technologies and connection distances gives system designers the flexibility to meet unique AI factory deployment needs.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A Hardware Ecosystem for Next-Generation AI Factories&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br /&gt;
NVIDIA and Cisco are collaborating with TE Connectivity and Amphenol to build USFP cages, connectors and modules, with additional partners expected to join. The shared form factor gives suppliers a common foundation for developing high-density pluggable infrastructure for 400Gb/s-per-lane fabrics to build a robust ecosystem for AI factory builders.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The collaboration builds on &lt;a href="https://newsroom.cisco.com/c/r/newsroom/en/us/a/y2026/m08/cisco-secure-ai-factory-nvidia-rack-scale.html" rel="nofollow" target="_blank" title="NVIDIA and Cisco’s existing work"&gt;NVIDIA and Cisco&amp;rsquo;s existing work&lt;/a&gt; to ensure NVIDIA Spectrum-X&amp;trade; Ethernet networking and Cisco Silicon One-based Ethernet networks work together seamlessly, simplifying AI infrastructure deployment for enterprises, neoclouds and sovereign clouds.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;NVIDIA and Cisco plan to create an open industry specification for USFP through an upcoming community-led multi-source project.&lt;/p&gt;
]]&gt;</content><categories><category>Press Releases</category></categories><modDate>Mon, 12 Oct 2026 15:05:42 GMT</modDate><relatedPages></relatedPages><description><![CDATA[NVIDIA and Cisco today announced plans for Ultra-Dense Small Form Factor Pluggable (USFP), a new high-density 400Gb/s-per-lane optical module designed to equip the hardware ecosystem for the next generation of AI factories using pluggable transceivers.]]></description><enclosure url="https://iprsoftwaremedia.com/219/files/202610/bb0658e6668adfadaaf0477f22795d99/ultra-dense-small-form-factor-pluggable.jpg" length="320326" type="image/jpeg"></enclosure><guid isPermaLink="true">https://nvidianews.nvidia.com/news/nvidia-and-cisco-introduce-new-pluggable-optics-form-factor-to-scale-ai-factories</guid><pubDate>Mon, 12 Oct 2026 15:00:00 GMT</pubDate></item><item><title>Into the Omniverse: How Developers Turn Ideas Into Simulations With Frontier AI Agents</title><link>https://blogs.nvidia.com/blog/developers-simulations-frontier-ai-agents/</link><media:content url="https://iprsoftwaremedia.com/219/files/202610/016b788b2d35ad703c42051807c2a4f2/6ac805fa3d63329b7859cf27_omniverse-overall-ov-x-astra-1920x1080-1/omniverse-overall-ov-x-astra-1920x1080-1_thmb.jpg?v=fa6d3afa-3fb1-41a9-a244-d472dfcb6b55" fileSize="20074565" type="video/mp4"></media:content><contentType>releases</contentType><image>&lt;img src="https://iprsoftwaremedia.com/219/files/202610/016b788b2d35ad703c42051807c2a4f2/6ac805fa3d63329b7859cf27_omniverse-overall-ov-x-astra-1920x1080-1/omniverse-overall-ov-x-astra-1920x1080-1_thmb.jpg?v=fa6d3afa-3fb1-41a9-a244-d472dfcb6b55" alt="omniverse-overall-ov-x-astra-1920x1080-1" align="left" hspace="15" vspace="5" /&gt;</image><subtitle></subtitle><categories><category>Blogs</category></categories><modDate>Thu, 08 Oct 2026 21:07:09 GMT</modDate><relatedPages></relatedPages><description><![CDATA[Turning a simulation idea into a working application means assembling assets, connecting physics and rendering, and checking that the scene behaves as intended. Developers are combining frontier AI models with NVIDIA Omniverse libraries to help carry out that work — building applications for exploring scenarios, investigating failures and improving designs. Developers direct AI agents through […]]]></description><author>NVIDIA Writers</author><guid isPermaLink="true">https://blogs.nvidia.com/blog/developers-simulations-frontier-ai-agents/</guid><pubDate>Thu, 08 Oct 2026 21:06:35 GMT</pubDate></item><item><title>NVIDIA Commits $1 Billion to Advance US Science Over the Next Five Years</title><link>https://nvidianews.nvidia.com/news/nvidia-commits-1-billion-to-advance-us-science-over-the-next-five-years</link><media:content url="https://iprsoftwaremedia.com/219/files/20224/6296531eb3aed3741918b6b5_DH1L4415-HDR-20220527-r5/DH1L4415-HDR-20220527-r5_thmb.jpg?v=dba29dde-5a9b-4ac8-bf58-a0b78da89547" fileSize="5094489" type="image/jpeg"></media:content><contentType>releases</contentType><image>&lt;img src="https://iprsoftwaremedia.com/219/files/20224/6296531eb3aed3741918b6b5_DH1L4415-HDR-20220527-r5/DH1L4415-HDR-20220527-r5_thmb.jpg?v=dba29dde-5a9b-4ac8-bf58-a0b78da89547" alt="NVIDIA Voyager" align="left" hspace="15" vspace="5" /&gt;</image><subtitle>Commitments Will Strengthen Fields Critical for US Leadership Including Quantum Computing, Healthcare and Energy Security</subtitle><content>&lt;![CDATA[&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;News Summary:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul type="disc"&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;NVIDIA announces commitments valued at $1 billion to advance U.S. science over the next five years, at a Washington event convening U.S. officials, industry leaders and members of the science community.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;This builds on longstanding collaboration between NVIDIA and national labs, spanning two decades.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;NVIDIA today announced commitments valued at $1 billion to build out the United States&amp;rsquo; capacity for super intelligence research and development in fields critical for U.S. leadership, including quantum computing, healthcare and energy security.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The announcement was made during the Science: A New Golden Age event in Washington, D.C., where U.S. officials, industry leaders and members of the science community convened on the public-private collaborations needed to bolster scientific exploration.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&amp;ldquo;President Trump&amp;rsquo;s Genesis Mission is launching a new golden age of American discovery,&amp;rdquo; said Jensen Huang, founder and CEO of NVIDIA. &amp;ldquo;With a $1 billion investment, NVIDIA is putting advanced Super Intelligence in the hands of America&amp;rsquo;s scientists to accelerate breakthroughs in medicine, energy and materials. This is how America turns scientific leadership into industrial leadership, and innovation into jobs and opportunity for generations.&amp;rdquo;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;During the event, the U.S. Office of Science and Technology Policy celebrated the expansion of the Genesis Mission, of which NVIDIA is a leading industry partner. In response, NVIDIA has invited members of the science community to collaborate in R&amp;amp;D using compute and super intelligence infrastructure resources to accelerate scientific discovery and promote U.S. innovation.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strengthening US Leadership in Scientific Discovery&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br /&gt;
Over the next five years, NVIDIA will commit $1 billion to the advancement of super intelligence for science and quantum computing across the U.S. through support of the nation&amp;rsquo;s higher-education research institutions, investments in accelerating American quantum leadership and support for cloud service providers bolstering U.S. government mission needs.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;NVIDIA is also a collaborator on a number of the phase 2 Genesis Mission awards announced today at the event, including projects in quantum computing, fusion, accelerator design and microelectronics.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;NVIDIA has collaborated with U.S. national labs for more than two decades. Last year, it announced its partnership with the U.S. Department of Energy (DOE) on the Genesis Mission, which includes &lt;a href="https://nvidianews.nvidia.com/news/nvidia-oracle-us-department-of-energy-ai-supercomputer-scientific-discovery" rel="nofollow" target="_blank" title=""&gt;&lt;u&gt;NVIDIA&amp;rsquo;s work to build the department&amp;rsquo;s largest supercomputer for scientific research&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/a&gt; at Argonne National Laboratory. This is in addition to supporting &lt;a href="https://nvidianews.nvidia.com/news/nvidia-partners-ai-infrastructure-america" rel="nofollow" target="_blank" title=""&gt;&lt;u&gt;seven new systems&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/a&gt; across Argonne and Los Alamos National Laboratories, accelerating the DOE&amp;rsquo;s mission of driving technological leadership.&lt;/p&gt;
]]&gt;</content><categories><category>Press Releases</category></categories><modDate>Thu, 08 Oct 2026 14:35:20 GMT</modDate><relatedPages></relatedPages><description><![CDATA[NVIDIA today announced commitments valued at $1 billion to build out the United States’ capacity for super intelligence research and development in fields critical for U.S. leadership, including quantum computing, healthcare and energy security.]]></description><guid isPermaLink="true">https://nvidianews.nvidia.com/news/nvidia-commits-1-billion-to-advance-us-science-over-the-next-five-years</guid><pubDate>Thu, 08 Oct 2026 14:31:00 GMT</pubDate></item><item><title>Rally Up: ‘Gears of War: E-Day’ Launches on GeForce NOW</title><link>https://blogs.nvidia.com/blog/geforce-now-thursday-gears-of-war-e-day/</link><media:content url="https://iprsoftwaremedia.com/219/files/202610/14fc8824076bdbffd0180b4d98e2a79b/6ac794223d6332663e580326_gfn-thursday-10-8-blog-1920x1080-logo-842x450/gfn-thursday-10-8-blog-1920x1080-logo-842x450_thmb.jpg?v=7dd5c271-5882-4cc5-9a64-7cb2b537e175" fileSize="92094" type="image/jpeg"></media:content><contentType>releases</contentType><image>&lt;img src="https://iprsoftwaremedia.com/219/files/202610/14fc8824076bdbffd0180b4d98e2a79b/6ac794223d6332663e580326_gfn-thursday-10-8-blog-1920x1080-logo-842x450/gfn-thursday-10-8-blog-1920x1080-logo-842x450_thmb.jpg?v=7dd5c271-5882-4cc5-9a64-7cb2b537e175" alt="gfn-thursday-10-8-blog-1920x1080-logo-842x450" align="left" hspace="15" vspace="5" /&gt;</image><subtitle></subtitle><categories><category>Blogs</category></categories><modDate>Thu, 08 Oct 2026 13:01:25 GMT</modDate><relatedPages></relatedPages><description><![CDATA[Gears of War: E-Day leads the charge on GeForce NOW this week, bringing Marcus Fenix and Dom Santiago’s first fight against the Locust Horde to the cloud with GeForce RTX-powered performance. A new way to join the action is also coming: Fire TV users will soon be able to purchase GeForce NOW memberships directly through […]]]></description><author>GeForce NOW Community</author><guid isPermaLink="true">https://blogs.nvidia.com/blog/geforce-now-thursday-gears-of-war-e-day/</guid><pubDate>Thu, 08 Oct 2026 13:00:46 GMT</pubDate></item><item><title>NVIDIA, Microsoft Kick Off a New Beginning for Windows PCs with RTX Spark and AI Agents</title><link>https://blogs.nvidia.com/blog/local-ai-rtx-spark-microsoft-windows-event/</link><media:content url="https://iprsoftwaremedia.com/219/files/202111/618c4510ed6ae54e51b85162_nv-blog-preview-1280x680-1-842x450/nv-blog-preview-1280x680-1-842x450_thmb.jpg?v=7f16f52c-ffb3-4f7e-a25d-61580f0dc38c" fileSize="75869" type="image/jpeg"></media:content><contentType>releases</contentType><image>&lt;img src="https://iprsoftwaremedia.com/219/files/202111/618c4510ed6ae54e51b85162_nv-blog-preview-1280x680-1-842x450/nv-blog-preview-1280x680-1-842x450_thmb.jpg?v=7f16f52c-ffb3-4f7e-a25d-61580f0dc38c" alt="nv-blog-preview-1280x680-1-842x450" align="left" hspace="15" vspace="5" /&gt;</image><subtitle></subtitle><categories><category>Blogs</category></categories><modDate>Wed, 07 Oct 2026 18:45:18 GMT</modDate><relatedPages></relatedPages><description><![CDATA[At a Microsoft event in San Francisco on Wednesday, Jensen Huang and Satya Nadella outlined how NVIDIA and Microsoft are co-engineering hardware and software for AI agents to run on Windows PCs. NVIDIA was founded because of Windows, Huang said. Now AI agents are coming to Windows. “If you look at the entire journey of […]]]></description><author>Gerardo Delgado</author><guid isPermaLink="true">https://blogs.nvidia.com/blog/local-ai-rtx-spark-microsoft-windows-event/</guid><pubDate>Wed, 07 Oct 2026 18:45:28 GMT</pubDate></item><item><title>Why Telecom Operators Are Building Their AI Strategy on Open Models</title><link>https://blogs.nvidia.com/blog/telecom-operators-open-models/</link><media:content url="https://iprsoftwaremedia.com/219/files/202610/642defbc7620d6020affe8cefb3c4b63/6ac4f1233d6332553de4d26a_image1-842x450/image1-842x450_thmb.jpg?v=90670c5a-8145-45a9-95e0-106ffbdc603b" fileSize="120535" type="image/png"></media:content><contentType>releases</contentType><image>&lt;img src="https://iprsoftwaremedia.com/219/files/202610/642defbc7620d6020affe8cefb3c4b63/6ac4f1233d6332553de4d26a_image1-842x450/image1-842x450_thmb.jpg?v=90670c5a-8145-45a9-95e0-106ffbdc603b" alt="image1-842x450" align="left" hspace="15" vspace="5" /&gt;</image><subtitle></subtitle><categories><category>Blogs</category></categories><modDate>Tue, 06 Oct 2026 13:01:27 GMT</modDate><relatedPages></relatedPages><description><![CDATA[Telecom operators are increasingly building their AI strategies on open models — and the reasons go beyond mere cost.  Open models give telcos the ability to trust, control and customize AI across their most critical workloads — from autonomous networks to customer care.  NVIDIA’s latest State of AI in Telecommunications report reflects this shift, with […]]]></description><author>Kanika Atri</author><guid isPermaLink="true">https://blogs.nvidia.com/blog/telecom-operators-open-models/</guid><pubDate>Tue, 06 Oct 2026 13:00:19 GMT</pubDate></item><item><title>From Scan to Treatment Plan, AI Helps Close Breast Cancer’s Deadliest Gaps</title><link>https://blogs.nvidia.com/blog/ai-breast-cancer-startups/</link><media:content url="https://iprsoftwaremedia.com/219/files/202610/b1939cc201efc5ee8ba102ec352c5311/6ac39fbe3d6332b35f1da8a7_AdobeStock_422714256_BCAMheader-842x450/AdobeStock_422714256_BCAMheader-842x450_thmb.jpg?v=24711c28-a239-42ba-a70d-9ac1f41ba238" fileSize="68423" type="image/jpeg"></media:content><contentType>releases</contentType><image>&lt;img src="https://iprsoftwaremedia.com/219/files/202610/b1939cc201efc5ee8ba102ec352c5311/6ac39fbe3d6332b35f1da8a7_AdobeStock_422714256_BCAMheader-842x450/AdobeStock_422714256_BCAMheader-842x450_thmb.jpg?v=24711c28-a239-42ba-a70d-9ac1f41ba238" alt="AdobeStock_422714256_BCAMheader-842x450" align="left" hspace="15" vspace="5" /&gt;</image><subtitle></subtitle><categories><category>Blogs</category></categories><modDate>Mon, 05 Oct 2026 20:42:23 GMT</modDate><relatedPages></relatedPages><description><![CDATA[Breast cancer is the most commonly diagnosed cancer among American women — yet the gaps in care are wide. A majority of women over age 40 skip the recommended annual screening. Radiologists are reading more mammograms with fewer colleagues. And when a diagnosis arrives, the tests that inform treatment can take weeks to return results.  […]]]></description><author>Chelsea Sumner</author><guid isPermaLink="true">https://blogs.nvidia.com/blog/ai-breast-cancer-startups/</guid><pubDate>Mon, 05 Oct 2026 13:00:57 GMT</pubDate></item><item><title>NVIDIA DGX Spark 64GB Gives Developers More Ways to Build and Scale Local AI</title><link>https://blogs.nvidia.com/blog/local-ai-dgx-spark-64gb-sync/</link><media:content url="https://iprsoftwaremedia.com/219/files/202503/67d2d7233d6332977ae163b9_nv-blog-1280x680-1-842x450/nv-blog-1280x680-1-842x450_thmb.jpg?v=a123af9d-8d9d-4a99-91d8-2cf5361f2445" fileSize="81880" type="image/jpeg"></media:content><contentType>releases</contentType><image>&lt;img src="https://iprsoftwaremedia.com/219/files/202503/67d2d7233d6332977ae163b9_nv-blog-1280x680-1-842x450/nv-blog-1280x680-1-842x450_thmb.jpg?v=a123af9d-8d9d-4a99-91d8-2cf5361f2445" alt="nv-blog-1280x680-1-842x450" align="left" hspace="15" vspace="5" /&gt;</image><subtitle></subtitle><categories><category>Blogs</category></categories><modDate>Fri, 02 Oct 2026 13:01:44 GMT</modDate><relatedPages></relatedPages><description><![CDATA[Local AI is becoming more useful by the token. As AI agents move from experiments into everyday development, increasingly capable open models are shrinking to fit on more devices, giving builders more to run locally.  Coming this month, NVIDIA DGX Spark will be available with 64GB of unified memory from top manufacturer partners — Acer, […]]]></description><author>Allen Bourgoyne</author><guid isPermaLink="true">https://blogs.nvidia.com/blog/local-ai-dgx-spark-64gb-sync/</guid><pubDate>Fri, 02 Oct 2026 13:00:39 GMT</pubDate></item><item><title>How NVIDIA GPUs Help Accelerate OpenAI’s GPT-6 Astra Ultrafast</title><link>https://blogs.nvidia.com/blog/gpus-openai-gpt-6-astra-ultrafast/</link><media:content url="https://iprsoftwaremedia.com/219/files/202610/d1cb38eec4ee290ac0fea39ce15a35d8/6abef08d3d6332a948f30c2f_twitter-gif-2104993966043320759-v5-842x450/twitter-gif-2104993966043320759-v5-842x450_thmb.jpg?v=f8092bd5-856c-4205-8168-bfcda2d24714" fileSize="251532" type="image/png"></media:content><contentType>releases</contentType><image>&lt;img src="https://iprsoftwaremedia.com/219/files/202610/d1cb38eec4ee290ac0fea39ce15a35d8/6abef08d3d6332a948f30c2f_twitter-gif-2104993966043320759-v5-842x450/twitter-gif-2104993966043320759-v5-842x450_thmb.jpg?v=f8092bd5-856c-4205-8168-bfcda2d24714" alt="twitter-gif-2104993966043320759-v5-842x450" align="left" hspace="15" vspace="5" /&gt;</image><subtitle></subtitle><categories><category>Blogs</category></categories><modDate>Thu, 01 Oct 2026 23:45:21 GMT</modDate><relatedPages></relatedPages><description><![CDATA[GPT-6 Astra Ultrafast, running on NVIDIA Blackwell GPUs, is available now in the OpenAI API and to eligible ChatGPT Work and Codex users.  Accelerated by inference optimizations through OpenAI’s models that tap into the capabilities of the NVIDIA Blackwell architecture, Ultrafast offers up to 8x faster token generation than the Astra Standard mode. For developers, […]]]></description><author>Dion Harris</author><guid isPermaLink="true">https://blogs.nvidia.com/blog/gpus-openai-gpt-6-astra-ultrafast/</guid><pubDate>Thu, 01 Oct 2026 23:44:13 GMT</pubDate></item><item><title>Fall Into 25 New Games on GeForce NOW This October</title><link>https://blogs.nvidia.com/blog/geforce-now-thursday-october-2026-games-list/</link><media:content url="https://iprsoftwaremedia.com/219/files/202610/8c18cff77482434dbac5135b5d20689f/6abe59c33d6332bdba437e62_GFN_Thursday-Oct_1-842x450/GFN_Thursday-Oct_1-842x450_thmb.jpg?v=b1ce4094-2b6d-413d-ae5f-ccc418dcbe24" fileSize="127402" type="image/jpeg"></media:content><contentType>releases</contentType><image>&lt;img src="https://iprsoftwaremedia.com/219/files/202610/8c18cff77482434dbac5135b5d20689f/6abe59c33d6332bdba437e62_GFN_Thursday-Oct_1-842x450/GFN_Thursday-Oct_1-842x450_thmb.jpg?v=b1ce4094-2b6d-413d-ae5f-ccc418dcbe24" alt="GFN_Thursday-Oct_1-842x450" align="left" hspace="15" vspace="5" /&gt;</image><subtitle></subtitle><categories><category>Blogs</category></categories><modDate>Thu, 01 Oct 2026 13:01:59 GMT</modDate><relatedPages></relatedPages><description><![CDATA[Spooky season is streaming in. Alongside falling leaves, pumpkin spice and everything nice, 25 new games are joining GeForce NOW throughout October, including six ready to play this week. From a new CONTROL Resonant reward for Performance and Ultimate members to The Witcher 3: Wild Hunt – Remastered joining the cloud, this GFN Thursday is […]]]></description><author>GeForce NOW Community</author><guid isPermaLink="true">https://blogs.nvidia.com/blog/geforce-now-thursday-october-2026-games-list/</guid><pubDate>Thu, 01 Oct 2026 13:00:54 GMT</pubDate></item><item><title>Productive, Durable, Fungible: How NVIDIA AI Factories Maximize Return on Investment</title><link>https://blogs.nvidia.com/blog/productive-durable-fungible-ai-factories/</link><media:content url="https://iprsoftwaremedia.com/219/files/202610/810a8175b65f5945603f8af1a6039432/6abe5a043d6332bec0d2cd2d_fungibility-blog-1280x680-1-842x450/fungibility-blog-1280x680-1-842x450_thmb.jpg?v=ee5f6585-1b63-483c-a624-b8a1a8451244" fileSize="70377" type="image/jpeg"></media:content><contentType>releases</contentType><image>&lt;img src="https://iprsoftwaremedia.com/219/files/202610/810a8175b65f5945603f8af1a6039432/6abe5a043d6332bec0d2cd2d_fungibility-blog-1280x680-1-842x450/fungibility-blog-1280x680-1-842x450_thmb.jpg?v=ee5f6585-1b63-483c-a624-b8a1a8451244" alt="fungibility-blog-1280x680-1-842x450" align="left" hspace="15" vspace="5" /&gt;</image><subtitle></subtitle><categories><category>Blogs</category></categories><modDate>Thu, 01 Oct 2026 13:03:04 GMT</modDate><relatedPages></relatedPages><description><![CDATA[AI factories are built by the megawatt, even by the gigawatt. Each megawatt factory costs roughly $60 million, and AI factory operators will only commit capital on that scale with a clear view of the return on investment. Three key things shape AI factory returns:  Earning capacity: What the factory could earn in a year […]]]></description><author>Shruti Koparkar</author><guid isPermaLink="true">https://blogs.nvidia.com/blog/productive-durable-fungible-ai-factories/</guid><pubDate>Thu, 01 Oct 2026 13:00:49 GMT</pubDate></item><item><title>NVIDIA Opens Applications for 2027–2028 Graduate Fellowships With Awards Up to $60,000</title><link>https://blogs.nvidia.com/blog/applications-open-graduate-fellowship-awards-2026/</link><media:content url="https://iprsoftwaremedia.com/219/files/202609/ee1928d508ca963c894784a02b6113fd/6abd40523d633214cb8a7db4_graduate-fellowship-2026-updated-842x450/graduate-fellowship-2026-updated-842x450_thmb.jpg?v=d8ac71cd-fe6d-4082-8263-cb768ed942f1" fileSize="594291" type="image/png"></media:content><contentType>releases</contentType><image>&lt;img src="https://iprsoftwaremedia.com/219/files/202609/ee1928d508ca963c894784a02b6113fd/6abd40523d633214cb8a7db4_graduate-fellowship-2026-updated-842x450/graduate-fellowship-2026-updated-842x450_thmb.jpg?v=d8ac71cd-fe6d-4082-8263-cb768ed942f1" alt="graduate-fellowship-2026-updated-842x450" align="left" hspace="15" vspace="5" /&gt;</image><subtitle></subtitle><categories><category>Blogs</category></categories><modDate>Wed, 30 Sep 2026 17:01:13 GMT</modDate><relatedPages></relatedPages><description><![CDATA[Bringing together the world’s brightest minds and the latest accelerated computing technology leads to powerful breakthroughs that help tackle some of the biggest research problems. To foster such innovation, the NVIDIA Graduate Fellowship Program provides grants, mentors and technical support to doctoral students doing outstanding research relevant to NVIDIA technologies. The program, in its 26th […]]]></description><author>Sharon Gibbons</author><guid isPermaLink="true">https://blogs.nvidia.com/blog/applications-open-graduate-fellowship-awards-2026/</guid><pubDate>Wed, 30 Sep 2026 17:00:21 GMT</pubDate></item><item><title>From Training to Production, NVIDIA and CoreWeave Close the Loop on Agentic AI</title><link>https://blogs.nvidia.com/blog/coreweave-agentic-ai-vera-rubin/</link><media:content url="https://iprsoftwaremedia.com/219/files/202609/c994f47c6b49141a96a67fed66981be3/6abd25513d633284ffca0d51_logo-lockup-corp-blog-coreweave-1280x680-1-842x450/logo-lockup-corp-blog-coreweave-1280x680-1-842x450_thmb.jpg?v=6db82ef4-6b4a-4ab3-a03a-5bf1d18cd178" fileSize="24668" type="image/png"></media:content><contentType>releases</contentType><image>&lt;img src="https://iprsoftwaremedia.com/219/files/202609/c994f47c6b49141a96a67fed66981be3/6abd25513d633284ffca0d51_logo-lockup-corp-blog-coreweave-1280x680-1-842x450/logo-lockup-corp-blog-coreweave-1280x680-1-842x450_thmb.jpg?v=6db82ef4-6b4a-4ab3-a03a-5bf1d18cd178" alt="logo-lockup-corp-blog-coreweave-1280x680-1-842x450" align="left" hspace="15" vspace="5" /&gt;</image><subtitle></subtitle><categories><category>Blogs</category></categories><modDate>Wed, 30 Sep 2026 15:06:01 GMT</modDate><relatedPages></relatedPages><description><![CDATA[Building on nearly a decade of co-engineering, CoreWeave has built NVIDIA compute, networking and software into a cloud purpose-built for AI that’s still returning on investment across multiple generations of deployment. Now, CoreWeave is bringing the next generation of NVIDIA infrastructure to production. At CoreWeave Fully Connected, running this week in San Francisco, CoreWeave announced […]]]></description><author>Stuart Pitts</author><guid isPermaLink="true">https://blogs.nvidia.com/blog/coreweave-agentic-ai-vera-rubin/</guid><pubDate>Wed, 30 Sep 2026 15:00:00 GMT</pubDate></item><item><title>NVIDIA Announces a $150 Billion Share Repurchase Authorization Increase</title><link>https://nvidianews.nvidia.com/news/nvidia-announces-a-150-billion-share-repurchase-authorization-increase</link><media:content url="https://iprsoftwaremedia.com/219/files/20224/6296531eb3aed3741918b6b5_DH1L4415-HDR-20220527-r5/DH1L4415-HDR-20220527-r5_thmb.jpg?v=dba29dde-5a9b-4ac8-bf58-a0b78da89547" fileSize="5094489" type="image/jpeg"></media:content><contentType>releases</contentType><image>&lt;img src="https://iprsoftwaremedia.com/219/files/20224/6296531eb3aed3741918b6b5_DH1L4415-HDR-20220527-r5/DH1L4415-HDR-20220527-r5_thmb.jpg?v=dba29dde-5a9b-4ac8-bf58-a0b78da89547" alt="NVIDIA Voyager" align="left" hspace="15" vspace="5" /&gt;</image><subtitle></subtitle><content>&lt;![CDATA[&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;News Summary:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul type="disc"&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;NVIDIA&amp;rsquo;s Board of Directors has authorized a $150 billion increase to the share repurchase program, raising the remaining total program to $235 billion.&lt;br /&gt;
	&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;This marks the largest share repurchase authorization increase in history.&lt;br /&gt;
	&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;NVIDIA today announced that its Board of Directors has authorized an additional $150 billion under the company&amp;rsquo;s existing share repurchase program, increasing the total remaining amount authorized to $235 billion.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The company expects to execute the total remaining program through fiscal year 2028.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&amp;ldquo;NVIDIA&amp;rsquo;s growth is being driven by a once-in-a-generation platform shift to AI and accelerated computing,&amp;rdquo; said Jensen Huang, founder and CEO of NVIDIA. &amp;ldquo;Our cash generation gives us the capacity to invest in the technologies that advance this transformation and return capital to shareholders. This authorization reflects our confidence in the long-term opportunity ahead.&amp;rdquo;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
]]&gt;</content><categories><category>Press Releases</category></categories><modDate>Mon, 28 Sep 2026 11:08:06 GMT</modDate><relatedPages></relatedPages><description><![CDATA[NVIDIA today announced that its Board of Directors has authorized an additional $150 billion under the company’s existing share repurchase program, increasing the total remaining amount authorized to $235 billion.]]></description><enclosure url="https://iprsoftwaremedia.com/219/files/20224/DH1L4415-HDR-20220527-r5.jpg" length="5094489" type="image/jpeg"></enclosure><guid isPermaLink="true">https://nvidianews.nvidia.com/news/nvidia-announces-a-150-billion-share-repurchase-authorization-increase</guid><pubDate>Mon, 28 Sep 2026 11:00:00 GMT</pubDate></item><item><title>NVIDIA Launches Open Agent Safety Platform to Secure Agents From Testing to Deployment</title><link>https://nvidianews.nvidia.com/news/open-agent-safety-platform</link><media:content url="https://iprsoftwaremedia.com/219/files/202609/c68dda94943a6e093074e9e88fd5ddef/6aba9c533d6332d60a0bb99a_nvidia-open-agent-safety-platform/nvidia-open-agent-safety-platform_thmb.png?v=f9cea0c6-00ad-4b7f-b0a0-6bc06b39af63" fileSize="261337" type="image/png"></media:content><contentType>releases</contentType><image>&lt;img src="https://iprsoftwaremedia.com/219/files/202609/c68dda94943a6e093074e9e88fd5ddef/6aba9c533d6332d60a0bb99a_nvidia-open-agent-safety-platform/nvidia-open-agent-safety-platform_thmb.png?v=f9cea0c6-00ad-4b7f-b0a0-6bc06b39af63" alt="NVIDIA Open Agent Safety Platform" align="left" hspace="15" vspace="5" /&gt;</image><subtitle>Open Software Platform and Reference System Design Brings Together Industry, Researchers and Public-Sector Organizations to Set Safer Boundaries for AI Agents, Share Best Practices and Foster International Cooperation to Raise the Bar for Safer AI Agent Deployment</subtitle><content>&lt;![CDATA[&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;News Summary:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul type="disc"&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;NVIDIA Open Agent Safety Platform consists of NVIDIA OpenShell open source software and the NVIDIA Sentry reference system design that enables full-stack governance and control across software and the hardware, compute and robotics systems that run agents.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;OpenShell software provides a secure runtime boundary that traces all actions and enforces policy as agents run on NVIDIA Vera CPUs. As open source software, OpenShell can be extended to work with third-party compute platforms, including those from Arm and Intel.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Sentry adds an out-of-band watchdog that runs on NVIDIA BlueField-4 DPUs to continuously monitor agent behavior. Sentry can quarantine agents that attempt to move outside their boundaries in milliseconds.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Industry leaders from across the AI ecosystem are joining NVIDIA to strengthen AI safety for every industry across the full stack of infrastructure, software, models and robotics &amp;mdash; including Anthropic, Cisco, CrowdStrike, Dell Technologies, Figure, HPE, Hugging Face, JPMorganChase, Microsoft, Palantir, Palo Alto Networks, Perplexity, Red Hat, Salesforce, SAP, Scale AI, ServiceNow and SpaceXAI.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;NVIDIA today announced&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href="https://www.nvidia.com/en-us/solutions/ai/agent-safety/" rel="nofollow" target="_blank" title=""&gt;&lt;u&gt;NVIDIA Open Agent Safety Platform&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/a&gt;, an open software platform and reference system design to strengthen AI security from agent testing to deployment, with full-stack governance and control across software and the hardware, compute and robotics systems that run agents.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Recent security incidents have underscored the need to equip organizations with open, customizable tools that enforce more control over long-running agents. Across these incidents, the pattern is the same &amp;mdash; the agent circumvented security controls at the application layer to complete its assigned task.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&amp;ldquo;AI&amp;rsquo;s extraordinary potential for society will only be realized if we solve AI safety,&amp;rdquo; said Jensen Huang, founder and CEO of NVIDIA. &amp;ldquo;As we continue to discover the frontier of AI capabilities, we must accelerate discovery at the frontier of AI safety. Safety and security require full-stack engineering. NVIDIA Open Agent Safety Platform brings together industry, researchers and public-sector organizations to share best practices, align on evaluation methods and foster international cooperation. Together, we can raise the bar for global AI safety.&amp;rdquo;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Open Agent Safety Platform Adds Control Across the Full Agent Stack &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br /&gt;
NVIDIA Open Agent Safety Platform enables full-stack governance and control across the software that runs agents, the hardware and compute layers that power their work, and the robotics systems that execute tasks in the physical world. Organizations can deploy elements of NVIDIA Open Agent Safety Platform according to their unique requirements.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;It includes &lt;a href="https://www.nvidia.com/en-us/ai/openshell/" rel="nofollow" target="_blank" title=""&gt;&lt;u&gt;NVIDIA OpenShell&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&amp;trade; secure runtime software that sets boundaries for agents running on CPUs. As agents take on more work across more systems, enterprises need an enforceable boundary outside of the model and agent harness. Now broadly available, &lt;a href="https://developer.nvidia.com/blog/add-runtime-controls-to-ai-agents-with-nvidia-openshell" rel="nofollow" target="_blank" title=""&gt;&lt;u&gt;OpenShell&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/a&gt; provides a secure runtime boundary for controlling how autonomous AI agents execute tasks across open and closed models.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;OpenShell delivers this protection with minimal overhead on &lt;a href="https://www.nvidia.com/en-us/data-center/vera-cpu/" rel="nofollow" target="_blank" title=""&gt;&lt;u&gt;NVIDIA Vera&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/a&gt;, the first purpose-built CPU for agentic AI. Together, OpenShell and Vera enable agents to operate securely while completing their work as quickly as possible. As open source software, OpenShell can also be extended to work with third-party compute platforms, including those from &lt;a href="https://newsroom.arm.com/blog/trusted-compute-foundation-agentic-ai" rel="nofollow" target="_blank" title=""&gt;&lt;u&gt;Arm&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/a&gt; and &lt;a href="https://www.intel.com/content/www/us/en/newsroom/news/data-center/intel-agent-toolkit-adds-nvidia-openshell-for-policy-enforced-sandboxes.html" rel="" target="_blank" title=""&gt;Intel&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The NVIDIA Open Agent Safety Platform reference system design features &lt;a href="https://developer.nvidia.com/blog/nvidia-open-agent-safety-platform-a-reference-for-continuous-in-silicon-agent-monitoring/" rel="nofollow" target="_blank" title=""&gt;&lt;u&gt;NVIDIA Sentry&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/a&gt;, an out-of-band watchdog that runs on &lt;a href="https://www.nvidia.com/en-us/networking/products/data-processing-unit/" rel="nofollow" target="_blank" title=""&gt;&lt;u&gt;NVIDIA BlueField&lt;sup&gt;&amp;reg;&lt;/sup&gt;-4&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/a&gt; DPUs to continuously monitor agent behavior. Sentry provides in-silicon security enforcement, meaning that if an AI agent attempts to move outside its software boundary, Sentry quarantines and stops it in milliseconds.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Running on BlueField-4 DPUs, Sentry continuously monitors agent activity and enforces security policies independently in silicon. It combines threat detection, hardware-based agent governance and enforcement and data access protection from an isolated, out-of-band trust domain that is responsive in real time and invisible to agents and attackers.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Sentry is built on &lt;a href="https://www.nvidia.com/en-us/networking/products/software/doca/" rel="nofollow" target="_blank" title=""&gt;&lt;u&gt;NVIDIA DOCA&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&amp;trade; software, which provides the programmable capabilities Sentry uses to inspect agent requests and responses, provide attested telemetry, verify agent identity and enforce granular, zero-trust access policies for data, tools, application programming interfaces and services.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Industry Leaders Strengthen Agent Security With NVIDIA&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br /&gt;
&lt;a href="https://claude.com/blog/giving-companies-more-control-over-their-ai-agents-with-nvidia" rel="" target="_blank" title=""&gt;Anthropic&lt;/a&gt; and NVIDIA have collaborated to bring additional layers of security and control to the agent stack. Claude Managed Agents establish a security boundary by running the agent loop in a separate server from the sandboxes where their work executes. Integrations with OpenShell and BlueField enable enterprises to enforce strict control over agent access through those sandboxes.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&amp;ldquo;Companies are giving AI agents more of their most important work, and they need to direct and verify what those agents do, especially in sensitive environments,&amp;rdquo; said Paul Smith, chief commercial officer of Anthropic. &amp;ldquo;Claude Managed Agents gives companies a clear view of what each agent is doing, and NVIDIA&amp;rsquo;s platform adds another layer of governance and control across hardware and software.&amp;rdquo;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;SpaceXAI is using NVIDIA Open Agent Safety Platform for Cursor coding agents and Grok models.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&amp;ldquo;As customers rely more on agents to get real work done, safety should be enforced outside the model by additional controls the agent can&amp;rsquo;t get past,&amp;rdquo; said Mike Nicolls, president at SpaceXAI. &amp;ldquo;Customers should be able to set those limits for Cursor and Grok and trust they will hold.&amp;rdquo;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Scale AI is working with NVIDIA to incorporate NVIDIA Open Agent Safety Platform technologies into the agentic infrastructure layer of Scale GenAI Portfolio.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&amp;ldquo;Scale AI is using the NVIDIA Open Agent Safety Platform reference design to build reliable agentic AI systems for our enterprise and government customers running mission-critical applications, with isolation, policy enforcement and auditability built in from the start,&amp;rdquo; said Francis deSouza, CEO of Scale AI. &amp;ldquo;We support agentic security with clear boundaries that define what agents can do, and controls that keep them operating within those permissions.&amp;rdquo;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.salesforce.com/blog/extending-admin-control-to-the-runtime-layer-with-nvidia-openshell-and-slack/" rel="" target="_blank" title=""&gt;Salesforce&lt;/a&gt; and NVIDIA have integrated OpenShell with Slack, enabling teams to manage OpenShell agent activity directly from Slack &amp;mdash; viewing agent activity and audit events, and approving or rejecting agent requests for additional permissions &amp;mdash; giving teams greater visibility and human oversight as agents work.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://news.sap.com/?p=247809" rel="nofollow" target="_blank" title=""&gt;&lt;u&gt;SAP&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/a&gt; is embedding OpenShell with Joule Studio runtime, part of the SAP Business AI Platform, to pair business oversight with runtime security. The company is also contributing engineering work to OpenShell and working with NVIDIA to advance interoperability standards through the &lt;a href="https://blogs.nvidia.com/blog/open-secure-ai-alliance/" rel="nofollow" target="_blank" title=""&gt;&lt;u&gt;Open Secure AI Alliance&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://newsroom.accenture.com/blogs/2026/accenture-helps-organizations-unlock-greater-ai-choice-and-control-with-open-weight-models" rel="nofollow" target="_blank" title=""&gt;&lt;u&gt;Accenture&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href="http://www.armadin.com/blog-posts/safe-autonomous-security-armadin-joins-nvidia-agent-safety-platform" rel="nofollow" target="_blank" title=""&gt;&lt;u&gt;Armadin&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href="https://community.cadence.com/cadence_blogs_8/b/corporate-news/posts/trusted-autonomy-with-cadence-ai-super-agents-and-nvidia-agent-safety-platform" rel="nofollow" target="_blank" title=""&gt;&lt;u&gt;Cadence&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/a&gt;, Cognition, &lt;a href="http://www.crowdstrike.com/en-us/blog/crowdstrike-nvidia-extend-security-across-ai-stack" rel="nofollow" target="_blank" title=""&gt;&lt;u&gt;CrowdStrike&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href="https://blogs.cisco.com/news/beyond-intelligence-how-trust-is-the-benchmark-that-matters-in-ai" rel="nofollow" target="_blank" title=""&gt;&lt;u&gt;Cisco&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/a&gt;, Dassault Syst&amp;egrave;mes, Deloitte, EY, Hugging Face, &lt;a href="https://newsroom.ibm.com/blog-building-trust-into-the-next-generation-of-ai-agents" rel="nofollow" target="_blank" title=""&gt;&lt;u&gt;IBM&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/a&gt;, Irregular, Perplexity, Microsoft, SAP, Scale AI, ServiceNow, Siemens, Synopsys, OpenClaw, Palantir and &lt;a href="https://www.paloaltonetworks.com/blog/2026/09/securing-ai-agents-at-scale-with-nvidia/" rel="nofollow" target="_blank" title=""&gt;&lt;u&gt;Palo Alto Networks&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/a&gt; are also among the over 100 organizations working with NVIDIA Open Agent Safety Platform technologies.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Robotics leaders &amp;mdash; such as Figure, &lt;a href="https://www.geckorobotics.com/news/nvidia-openshell" rel="nofollow" target="_blank" title=""&gt;&lt;u&gt;Gecko Robotics&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/a&gt; and Skild AI &amp;mdash; are also building with OpenShell to embed agent safety controls into autonomous systems that take action in the physical world.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Citi and JPMorganChase are among the financial services leaders collaborating with NVIDIA on shared open source agent safety technologies.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Energy leaders Hitachi Energy, EPRI, NextEra Energy, Quanta Services, SPP, Schneider Electric, Siemens Energy and Worley are among critical U.S. infrastructure providers working with NVIDIA Open Agent Safety Platform technologies.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Infrastructure software leaders &lt;a href="https://canonical.com/blog/charmed-openshell-alpha-release" rel="nofollow" target="_blank" title=""&gt;&lt;u&gt;Canonical&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href="http://suse.com/c/we-gave-our-agents-autonomy-heres-how-we-kept-control" rel="nofollow" target="_blank" title=""&gt;&lt;u&gt;SUSE&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/a&gt; and &lt;a href="https://www.redhat.com/en/blog/securing-ai-agents-requires-securing-systems-around-them" rel="nofollow" target="_blank" title=""&gt;&lt;u&gt;Red Hat&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/a&gt; are also integrating NVIDIA Open Agent Safety Platform into widely used software operating systems. Red Hat runs OpenShell and DOCA, both part of NVIDIA Open Agent Safety Platform, on Red Hat AI Factory with NVIDIA, a co-engineered, enterprise-grade AI solution for building, deploying and managing AI at scale across hybrid cloud environments.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;NVIDIA partners including &lt;a href="http://www.baseten.co/blog/announcing-carbon" rel="nofollow" target="_blank" title=""&gt;&lt;u&gt;Baseten&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/a&gt;, Cisco, CoreWeave, &lt;a href="https://www.dell.com/en-us/blog/a-new-era-of-ai-agents-demands-a-new-security-model/" rel="nofollow" target="_blank" title=""&gt;&lt;u&gt;Dell Technologies&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/a&gt;, GMI Cloud, &lt;a href="https://www.hpe.com/us/en/newsroom/blog-post/2026/09/hpe-and-nvidia-bring-secure-governed-agentic-ai-into-enterprise-production.html" rel="nofollow" target="_blank" title=""&gt;&lt;u&gt;HPE&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/a&gt;, HP Inc., Irregular, Lenovo, Microsoft, Nebius, Oracle Cloud Infrastructure, &lt;a href="https://learn-more.supermicro.com/data-center-stories/supermicro-supports-nvidia-open-agent-safety-platform" rel="nofollow" target="_blank" title=""&gt;&lt;u&gt;Supermicro&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/a&gt; and Together AI are among those offering AI infrastructure solutions that use and support NVIDIA Open Agent Safety Platform technologies to help customers run AI agents more securely.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Availability&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br /&gt;
NVIDIA Open Agent Safety Platform software, including OpenShell and skills, are available through the &lt;a href="https://docs.nvidia.com/openshell/about/why-open-shell" rel="nofollow" target="_blank" title=""&gt;&lt;u&gt;NVIDIA developer resources page&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/a&gt; and &lt;a href="https://github.com/NVIDIA/OpenShell" rel="nofollow" target="_blank" title=""&gt;&lt;u&gt;GitHub&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Ecosystem contributions such as NVIDIA Open Agent Safety Platform support the mission of the &lt;a href="https://blogs.nvidia.com/blog/open-secure-ai-alliance/" rel="nofollow" target="_blank" title=""&gt;&lt;u&gt;Open Secure AI Alliance&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/a&gt; as well as the broader AI safety and security community. Initiated by NVIDIA alongside over 120 leading organizations and governed by the Linux Foundation, the Open Secure AI Alliance strengthens AI agent security through open research, skills and tools, as well as projects like the &lt;a href="https://secureaialliance.org/#rfcs" rel="nofollow" target="_blank" title=""&gt;&lt;u&gt;Shared AI Findings Exchange&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/a&gt;, or SAFE.&lt;/p&gt;
]]&gt;</content><categories><category>Press Releases</category></categories><modDate>Mon, 05 Oct 2026 20:46:55 GMT</modDate><relatedPages></relatedPages><description><![CDATA[NVIDIA today announced NVIDIA Open Agent Safety Platform, an open software platform and reference system design to strengthen AI security from agent testing to deployment, with full-stack governance and control across software and the hardware, compute and robotics systems that run agents.]]></description><enclosure url="https://iprsoftwaremedia.com/219/files/202609/c68dda94943a6e093074e9e88fd5ddef/nvidia-open-agent-safety-platform.png" length="261337" type="image/png"></enclosure><guid isPermaLink="true">https://nvidianews.nvidia.com/news/open-agent-safety-platform</guid><pubDate>Mon, 28 Sep 2026 09:00:00 GMT</pubDate></item><item><title>How Open Science Can Help Researchers Prepare for the Next Pandemic</title><link>https://blogs.nvidia.com/blog/open-protein-dataset/</link><media:content url="https://iprsoftwaremedia.com/219/files/202609/306cbf129044501629326e0a7a1e125d/6ab52d223d63321fe4743d17_AF-0000000212056767-master-black-background-842x450/AF-0000000212056767-master-black-background-842x450_thmb.jpg?v=c4bfe338-2832-4d7f-957b-9d6c1481f447" fileSize="98987" type="image/png"></media:content><contentType>releases</contentType><image>&lt;img src="https://iprsoftwaremedia.com/219/files/202609/306cbf129044501629326e0a7a1e125d/6ab52d223d63321fe4743d17_AF-0000000212056767-master-black-background-842x450/AF-0000000212056767-master-black-background-842x450_thmb.jpg?v=c4bfe338-2832-4d7f-957b-9d6c1481f447" alt="AF-0000000212056767-master-black-background-842x450" align="left" hspace="15" vspace="5" /&gt;</image><subtitle></subtitle><categories><category>Blogs</category></categories><modDate>Thu, 24 Sep 2026 14:01:10 GMT</modDate><relatedPages></relatedPages><description><![CDATA[When COVID-19 emerged, scientists had a crucial advantage: Decades of prior research on coronaviruses meant they understood the virus’ key proteins well enough to design vaccines in record time. The next pandemic may not offer the same head start.  To help improve the odds, NVIDIA has joined a coalition of global research organizations, including Google […]]]></description><author>Anthony Costa</author><guid isPermaLink="true">https://blogs.nvidia.com/blog/open-protein-dataset/</guid><pubDate>Thu, 24 Sep 2026 14:00:50 GMT</pubDate></item></channel></rss>